    "pressure": {
      "file": "baghouse_dust_collector_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Filter on the outside, clean by a pulse",
      "description": "Dirty gas flows from outside to inside through the bags; dust builds a cake that itself becomes the fine filter (outlet dust often < 5–10 mg/Nm³). As the cake grows the pressure drop rises (typically held ≈ 1–1.5 kPa); the controller then fires a short compressed-air pulse down each row in turn, flexing the bags so the cake drops to the hopper. Air-to-cloth ratio (≈ 0.8–1.5 m/min for pulse-jet) sets the bag area. Watch temperature (bag limits), dew point (wet cake) and spark ignition risk.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
